---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { projectPath } from '../lib/readme';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Tomáš Samek: independent builder, Java and Rust, based in Prague.">
  <article class="post">
    <p class="label">About</p>
    <h1>Tomáš Samek</h1>
    <p class="post-summary">I build whatever I find interesting, and push it until it can't go any faster.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Right now that means a compile-time orchestrator for Java (<a href={projectPath('tiko-di')}>tiko-di</a>),
        a GPU renderer that delivers light instead of tracing it (<a href={projectPath('causal-cone-engine')}>causal-cone-engine</a>),
        a benchmark of how well AI coding agents actually build software (<a href={projectPath('llm-framework-benchmark')}>llm-framework-benchmark</a>),
        a memory server for AI agents that would rather say "I don't know" than guess (<a href={projectPath('trie-memory')}>trie-memory</a>),
        and, for my kids' school project, a toy physics visualization running in the browser (<a href={projectPath('tdm-demo')}>tdm-demo</a>).
      </p>
      <p>
        My strongest zone is the middle of the stack: real-time search and indexing, pluggable persistence,
        compile-time code generation, event-driven integration.
      </p>
      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>
        Independent since 2025. Before that, 19 years of Java, 13 of them at Oracle building enterprise platform
        infrastructure: real-time search, pluggable persistence, Jakarta EE. Based in Prague.
      </p>
      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/tomas-samek">GitHub</a> · <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/tomassamek">LinkedIn</a>.
        Side experiments in physics, linguistics and AI tooling live at <a href="https://github.com/jerry-samek">@jerry-samek</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
